<h2>Long transit, high-value trade</h2>
<p>North America is the longest sea route we ship at real volume — 25–35 days to the US East Coast — but the trade is correspondingly high-value: frozen shrimp above all, where the US is India's largest single-country market, plus basmati rice, psyllium husk and guar gum.</p>

<h2>Canada follows similar patterns to the US</h2>
<p>Where we don't yet have a dedicated Canada guide with verified country-specific figures, the underlying products and compliance principles are broadly consistent with US trade — Health Canada plays a comparable regulatory role to the FDA. If you're a Canadian buyer, <a href="/get-a-quote/">send us your requirement</a> and we'll quote directly.</p>

<h2>Compliance-first planning</h2>
<p>See our <a href="/markets/usa/">United States guide</a> for the detail on FSMA, FSVP and Seafood HACCP requirements that shape most North American food imports from India.</p>
